### Key behaviors
- `currentUser` starts as `null` → `SignInScreen` is shown instead of the calendar
- Session is React state only — resets on page refresh (by design, PRD F-17)
- All calendar data is shared across accounts (per-account isolation is out of scope, PRD §6)

### Component locations
- `client/context/AuthContext.tsx` — context, provider, hook, seeded accounts
- `client/components/auth/SignInScreen.tsx` — full-page account picker (PRD §4.1)
- `client/components/auth/ProfileMenu.tsx` — top-right dropdown (PRD §4.2)
- `client/components/calendar/TopBar.tsx` — avatar button that opens ProfileMenu

### Data flow
```
AuthProvider (Index.tsx → AuthGate)
  └── currentUser
       ├── null → <SignInScreen />
       └── Account → <CalendarLayout><CalendarApp /></CalendarLayout>
            └── TopBar uses useAuth() for avatar + ProfileMenu
                 └── ProfileMenu uses useAuth() for other accounts + signOut
```

### Adding new accounts
Add entries to the `SEEDED_ACCOUNTS` array in `AuthContext.tsx`. Each must have a unique `id` and `color`.
